## Why This Is Asked

Tests integration of multimodal signals into ICA, a practical scenario in automotive settings where visual cues help resolve source ambiguity and nonstationary noise.

## Key Concepts

- Multimodal ICA with audio-visual priors
- Online whitening and natural-gradient demixing
- Cross-bin permutation tracking using AV alignment cues
- Latency constraints for real-time automotive use
- Evaluation including SDR, SIR, and lip-sync accuracy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch for AV-regularized online ICA
let W = initialize(6,6);
for each frame t:
  X_t = frameAudio(mics, 32, 0.5);
  V_t = extractVisualFeatures(video);
  X_whitened = onlineWhiten(X_t);
  Y_t = W * X_whitened;
  W = naturalGradientUpdate(W, Y_t, V_t);
  permute = trackPermutationAV(Y_t, V_t);
  output = applyPermutation(Y_t, permute);
```

## Why This Is Asked
This scenario introduces motion-induced Doppler effects and wind noise, creating a practical non-stationary blind source separation problem. It tests understanding of online adaptation, cross-bin permutation alignment, and evaluation without perfect ground truth.

## Key Concepts
- Convolutive ICA in the STFT domain with online whitening
- Per-bin ICA versus joint diagonalization: latency versus frequency coherence trade-offs
- Cross-bin permutation using magnitude consistency and phase continuity cues
- Lightweight on-device evaluation using surrogate ground-truth signals

## Code Example
```javascript
function onlineWhiten(x, forgetFactor, state) {
  const alpha = forgetFactor;
  state.mean = alpha * state.mean + (1 - alpha) * x;
  state.cov = alpha * state.cov + (1 - alpha) * (x - state.mean).outer(x - state.mean);
  const whitened = (x - state.mean) * inv(sqrt(eigenvalues(state.cov)));
  return whitened;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle severe Doppler shifts that cause frequency warping beyond what standard STFT-based ICA can handle?
- What strategies would you use to evaluate separation quality on-device when no ground truth is available?
- How does the choice of STFT window length affect the Doppler robustness of the separation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a robust online ICA system for automotive cabins with real-time constraints and hardware faults.

## Key Concepts
- Online convolutive ICA with dynamic model order
- Robust whitening under missing sensors
- Dropout-aware demixer reinitialization
- Cross-bin permutation continuity across time
- Edge-device latency and evaluation strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: online ICA loop with dropout handling
while (streaming) {
  const frame = readFrame();
  const N = estimateSourceCount(frame);
  whiten(frame, N);
  if (dropoutDetected()) adjustDemixer(N);
  updateDemixer(N);
  alignPermutations(N);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate with synthetic vs real data when ground truth is unavailable?
- Which metrics best reflect real-time separation quality under dropout conditions?

