## Why This Is Asked

Car environments introduce dynamic geometry, intermittent sensor faults, and real-time constraints. This question probes the ability to design an online ICA solution that adapts to changing mixing, handles missing data gracefully, and maintains consistent source order over time.

## Key Concepts

- Online sliding-window ICA with adaptive whitening
- Kalman-style demixer updates on whitened data
- Missing-channel handling via subspace completion without reinitialization
- Permutation stability using short temporal memory and cross-frame non-Gaussianity cues
- Real-time latency targets and robust evaluation (ground-truth SDR/SIR, perceptual checks)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: online update for W on whitened data Xw
function onlineUpdate(W, Xw, lr) {
  const Y = W.dot(Xw);
  const e = gradientNonGaussianity(Y);
  return W.add(e.mul(lr).dot(Xw.transpose()));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you diagnose instability when sources cross or when dropouts occur?
- How would you scale to larger arrays with nonuniform sampling or asynchronous microphones?

## Why This Is Asked
Semi-supervised ICA in a mobile, real-world setting tests robustness to nonstationary channels and practical ambiguities that pure unsupervised methods struggle with. The calibration window anchors global alignment without sacrificing online adaptability.

## Key Concepts
- Semi-supervised ICA to resolve permutation/sign drift across bins
- Online whitening with forgetting factor in a convolutive model
- Adaptive selection between per-bin ICA and joint diagonalization
- Gain-drift compensation and robustification to wind/noise
- Ground-truth based evaluation (SDR/SIR) and lightweight diarization cues

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: anchorPermutation using calibration data
function anchorPermutation(calibStim, demixMatrix) {
  // compute permutation that best aligns calibStim with known sources
  // returns adjusted demixMatrix
  const perm = computeBestPermutation(calibStim, sourcesKnown);
  return applyPermutation(demixMatrix, perm);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect when to re-anchor permutation without labeled data?
- What are failure modes if wind noise mimics source spectra, and how mitigate?

